  },
  "body": "`try_set_portable_dir()` now returns whether it applied a portable dir, and the caller sets `APPIMAGE_PORTABLE_MODE=1` when any of portable home, share, config or cache is in use.\n\nThis gives the payload a single variable to detect portable mode instead of checking the `REAL_HOME`/`REAL_XDG_*` vars. First consumer is `anylinux.c`, which uses it to decide when `GSETTINGS_BACKEND=keyfile` is appropriate (pkgforge-dev/ghostty-appimage#158) \u2014 companion PR: pkgforge-dev/Anylinux-AppImages#839.\n\nOlder runtimes leave only the `REAL_*` vars, which `anylinux.c` keeps as a fallback, so this is not a hard dependency for it.\n\nDocumented in the `--help` output and README (both the RunImage and AppImage sections).\n\n---\nRequested by @Samueru-sama in the pi-discord agent session \u2014 transcript: https://talaria.qaidvoid.dev/api/sessions/2026-09-03T06-18-40-111Z_01a065eb-626f-76a2-b34d-5337020d5eb6/stream",
